From 58dc34160ff9ad688bcf8bb59e17b164033d7d7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raimondas Lencevicius <59739769+raimondasl@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:18:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] Record the model name each provider response reports

Step records stored only the requested model (request.model). The model
name the provider returns with each response, which can be more
specific than the request (a dated or versioned ID), was dropped, so a
run could not show which model actually served it. Gemini 3.8 Flash has
no dated snapshot ID, so the returned name is the only pin available.

- ModelResponse.reported_model is filled from the response's model field
  for Google Interactions, OpenAI Responses and OpenAI Chat Completions
  (the runtimes request.service_tier covers). Other runtimes leave it
  unset.
- step_NNN.json stores reported_model for the accepted response and
  compaction_NNN.json for the accepted summary; run_meta.json stores
  reported_models, the distinct names in order of first appearance.
- All three fields are omitted when no model name is reported, so
  existing files are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
